    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0414" n="410" xml:id="pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.516/608: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-27T11:00:00+08:00">May 27, 1939—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 27—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Nanking’s 31, May 9, 11 a.m.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d389-f1"/> Local press
                    reports establishment yesterday of Nanking branch of Huahsing Commercial Bank
                    “for the stabilization of the currency, opening up of remittances, expansion of
                    foreign trade, and realization of economic cooperation”. Other branches are
                    scheduled to be opened in mid-June at Soochow, Hangchow, Wusih, Chinkiang,
                    Wuhu.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
